  "rationale": "The national split is materially overstated. Indonesian rel and Malaysian Malay rel are both accepted terms for railway rail/track, while Malaysian landasan kereta api is also an accepted equivalent. The cue and sense are sound, but the two answers support a shared-synonym relationship rather than different-common-word. The empty contrast also fails to explain the overlap.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "Accurate: railway track refers to the rail/track on which trains travel.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=landasan",
        "https://jdih.kemenkeu.go.id/kamus-hukum/kereta-api?id=1e36432fea30b1bb46ae63696a38cd68"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer rel",
      "conclusion": "Correct and ordinary in Indonesian for a railway rail/track.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://tutur.taratsa.id/kata/rel/",
        "https://knkt.go.id/Repo/Files/Laporan/Perkeretaapian/2019/KNKT.19.03.01.02-Final-Report.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian answer landasan",
      "conclusion": "Correct, but not uniquely Malaysian: Malaysian dictionaries define landasan kereta api as the iron structure/place where trains travel and give rel as its equivalent.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=landasan+1",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=371752&keyword=rel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Cross-variety overlap and relation",
      "conclusion": "The relation different-common-word is incorrect or materially misleading. Malaysian rel is explicitly defined as railway rail/track, so rel overlaps across Indonesian and Malaysian Malay; landasan is also a Malaysian equivalent.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=371752&keyword=rel",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=landasan+1",
        "https://tutur.taratsa.id/kata/rel/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No genuine false-friend contrast is supported. The empty contrast should be replaced with an explicit overlap note, such as: rel is also valid in Malaysian Malay, while landasan kereta api is a Malaysian equivalent.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=371752&keyword=rel",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=landasan+1"
      ]
    }
  ]
